/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The core problem is that Amazon's marketplace prioritizes volume and revenue over user experience, leading to a cluttered and overwhelming product selection. This lack of curation and meaningful differentiation, combined with vague listings and ineffective personalised filtering systems, results in decision fatigue for users. The platform fails to support users in making informed choices, leaving them to navigate a complex and disorganized interface.)
/E (The core problem is that Amazon's marketplace prioritizes volume and revenue over user experience, leading to a cluttered and overwhelming product selection. This lack of curation and meaningful differentiation, combined with vague listings and ineffective personalised filtering systems, results in decision fatigue for users. The platform fails to support users in making informed choices, leaving them to navigate a complex and disorganized interface.)
